      "recommendation": "Run 2 needs ONE new capture run and it is cheap: teacher-forced per-token paired capture over the EXISTING 2560 saved token streams (target/latentmesh-runs/s2c/token-streams.jsonl) — no regeneration. Spec: for each row, prefill prompt+gen through sender (taps L18, L24) and receiver (taps L14, L19), dump per-token f32 rows for the generated span only (719,115 tokens; ~20.6 GB total across 4 layer files; ~5-15 min wall on the RTX 5080, vs ~2.5 GPU-h if regenerated). Modify src/capture.rs to return the pre-pooling span rows tensor alongside pooled; write ragged concatenated [T_i x dim] blocks per layer plus one shared u64 offsets index (T_i is identical across models per item by the tokenizer-parity gate) so a Rust loop can memmap2 + reinterpret &[f32] zero-copy. Capture ALL 2560 rows — the 13 probe-overlap rows are excluded in the TRAINING loop, not the capture, so the data asset stays complete and the discipline is auditable. Split discipline: (1) apply fit_holdout_split(2560, FIT_SPLIT_SEED=0x24C0_DE03) FIRST to preserve frozen-seed comparability with S2c, THEN drop the 13 probe rows (69, 683, 824, 1258, 1281, 1346, 1577, 1586, 1647, 2052, 2058, 2078, 2529) from whichever side they land in, recording the excluded list in the run-2 receipt; (2) split by ITEM, never by token — tokens within an item are correlated and a token-level split is leakage; (3) disclose that n_fit falls to ~2037-2048, technically below the d_sender=2048 n>d gate, noting that gate was a linear-identifiability constraint that does not carry the same meaning for MLP/GRNN adapters but must be stated; (4) do not draw a fresh probe set — that would contradict ADR-023's 'statistical protocol stays frozen' and is a coordinator/ADR-deviation decision, not a scout call. FIRST ACTION before any run-2 work: copy token-streams.jsonl (and s2c manifest + receipt) out of target/ to a durable location — it is the sole 4.75 MB encoding of ~2.5 GPU-h of generations and 'cargo clean' deletes it.",
